From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:52:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 101/117] media: iris: report enough capture buffers for AV1
 and VP9

After the reconfig event the driver reports the firmware's minimum
capture buffer count, which for AV1 and VP9 can be far below the number
of pictures the codec keeps as references (4 in split mode). Clients that
size their pool from min_number_of_capture_buffers then recycle surfaces
the firmware still references: frames come back late and the GStreamer
v4l2 decoder drops them.

Keep a floor that covers the reference set: 32 for AV1, the number the
VA-API frontend already requests, and 12 for VP9.

Found and measured by TheMojoMan (erhai iris tree faa3a3353a82, "keep at
least 32 capture buffers for AV1/VP9", no Signed-off-by); re-implemented
for our output_min_count(), which has no split-mode branch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_buffer.c  | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_buffer.c
index 7b78e461cb868..2f8ddd6bec38b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_buffer.c
@@ -2456,9 +2456,22 @@ static int output_min_count(struct iris_inst *inst)
 {
 	int output_min_count = 4;
 
-	/* fw_min_count > 0 indicates reconfig event has already arrived */
-	if (inst->fw_min_count)
+	/*
+	 * fw_min_count > 0 indicates reconfig event has already arrived.
+	 * For AV1 and VP9 the firmware can report far fewer buffers than the
+	 * codec keeps as references (4 in split mode); a client that sizes
+	 * its pool from that recycles surfaces the firmware still uses, and
+	 * frames come back late (GStreamer then drops them). Keep a floor
+	 * that covers the reference set: 32 for AV1, as the VA-API frontend
+	 * already requests, and 12 for VP9.
+	 */
+	if (inst->fw_min_count) {
+		if (inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1)
+			return max_t(u32, inst->fw_min_count, 32);
+		if (inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9)
+			return max_t(u32, inst->fw_min_count, 12);
 		return inst->fw_min_count;
+	}
 
 	if (inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9)
 		output_min_count = 9;
-- 
